From: nn <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH] beagley-ai: U-Boot binds only main_rti0 (nn trial watchdog)

With CONFIG_WDT on, initr_watchdog probes every watchdog node; probing the
per-core RTIs main_rti1..3 left cores 1-3 unable to come online in Linux.
Disable them (and main_rti15) in U-Boot's DT only.

---
--- a/arch/arm/dts/k3-am67a-beagley-ai-u-boot.dtsi	2026-09-16 04:22:28.536920371 +0800
+++ b/arch/arm/dts/k3-am67a-beagley-ai-u-boot.dtsi	2026-09-16 04:22:28.540920415 +0800
@@ -259,3 +259,28 @@
 	};
 };
 #endif /* CONFIG_TARGET_J722S_A53_BEAGLEY_AI */
+
+/*
+ * nn layout ab-v1, trial watchdog (CONFIG_WDT + WDT_K3_RTI): U-Boot's WDT
+ * uclass probes EVERY watchdog node at start-up (initr_watchdog), powering
+ * each RTI's domain through TI SCI.  With the per-A53-core RTIs main_rti1..3
+ * taken that way, the kernel's PSCI CPU_ON for cores 1-3 failed ("CPUn:
+ * failed to come online") and the board ran single-core (2026-09-16).
+ * nn_boot only ever arms main_rti0; this is U-Boot's own DT -- the kernel
+ * boots with the dtb from the slot's /boot, which keeps all of them.
+ */
+&main_rti1 {
+	status = "disabled";
+};
+
+&main_rti2 {
+	status = "disabled";
+};
+
+&main_rti3 {
+	status = "disabled";
+};
+
+&main_rti15 {
+	status = "disabled";
+};
